FerrionOS change to Mesa (MIT license, kept), made against both the fork the recipe pins (redox-24.0 at 9850ea1ad7d687240757ebf9a73760ceb4ba28a9) and Mesa 26.3.1 (fec8830e9c94b1d67f3d8469467d5529fb2978cd), whose sync_wait is the same. When poll is interrupted, sync_wait takes the time poll used off the remaining timeout; it subtracted the end's nanoseconds from themselves, so a wait interrupted again and again before a whole second had passed never ran out. It now subtracts the start's nanoseconds.

diff --git a/src/util/libsync.h b/src/util/libsync.h
index b22b75a..fcf914a 100644
--- a/src/util/libsync.h
+++ b/src/util/libsync.h
@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@ static inline int sync_wait(int fd, int timeout)
 			return -1;
 		}
 		timeout -= (poll_end.tv_sec - poll_start.tv_sec) * 1000 +
-			(poll_end.tv_nsec - poll_end.tv_nsec) / 1000000;
+			(poll_end.tv_nsec - poll_start.tv_nsec) / 1000000;
 	} while (ret == -1 && (errno == EINTR || errno == EAGAIN));
 
 	return ret;
